  "period_note": "Solo basis. Own contemporaneous annual report: 'Five Year's Performance of RBL' table (own/current-year column, fully self-consistent) plus Note 7.10-7.11 and the Capital Adequacy disclosure's audit-qualification-style footnote. This is the only year in the archive whose reported classified-loan ratio (21.19%) reproduces EXACTLY from classified loans / gross loans as reported (92,247,648,228 / 435,400,773,715 = 21.19%) - no gap, unlike every other year FY2015-FY2021. Provision shortfall (loans+OBS): required 71,661,343,186 Taka vs. maintained 17,273,688,220 Taka (maintained derived as required + reported shortfall of -54,387,654,966 Taka = BDT 5,438.77 crore; basis: calculated). The bank's own Capital Adequacy note additionally discloses a much larger COMBINED shortfall across all asset categories - loans BDT 6,940.00cr required vs 1,683.52cr maintained, off-balance-sheet 226.13cr vs 43.85cr, other assets 685.96cr vs 261.95cr, investments 278.63cr vs 94.50cr, NBFI(BIFC) 50.00cr vs 50.00cr - for a total required provision of BDT 8,180.72 crore against BDT 2,133.81 crore maintained, i.e. a shortfall of BDT 6,046.91 crore (Bangladesh Bank forbearance granted per letter dated 27 April 2023, deferred to finalization of the FY2023 financial statements). This all-asset-category figure is not broken into its own line item here (only the loans+OBS component is, for consistency with other years) but is central to insights.json: against reported total equity of just 1,634.67 crore, an all-in shortfall of 6,046.91 crore would be roughly 3.7x the bank's entire equity base if recognized.",
